	 <h3>Retaining Walls</h3>
	 <p>One of the most essential components of waterproofing is for below ground structures.It is very expensive to rectify water damage in retaining walls.Therefore it is mandatory to apply the correct principles so the membrane system is sustainable for the long term.Retaining wall is used for practice and aesthetic purposes.Common outcomes are a- providing terraces to sloping sites b- create a presentable garden which may not be usable otherwise and c-to free up and generate more usable space.Therefore all retaining walls have to be strong safe and trouble free.Retaining walls main job is to prevent the soil from spilling on to lower levels and retain the structure by controlling erosion redirecting water and preventing land slips.Waterproofing helps reduce hydro-static pressure and also protects the back of the wall from moisture.If this is not done properly moisture could seep through the walls leading to discoloring and affecting the integrity of the wall. </p>
	
	 
